# Instruction Fetch Mechanism

The Instruction Fetch Mechanism encompasses the processes and interfaces required to retrieve instructions and associated data from memory into the execution unit, operating within the context of the overall pipeline structure.

## Overview

The mechanism defines how the system handles the core tasks of instruction fetching, prediction, and memory access interfaces related to instructions, specifically how these operations interact with the pipeline stages and instruction execution cycles.</data>
