  <data key="d7">## Documents
- [[summaries/memory]] (short) — This page summarizes the Graphify topic cluster for 'memory' and provides OpenKB curation hints.
- [[summaries/pipeline_details_rst]] (short) — This document serves as a source map detailing the specific structure, stages, and instruction types within the pipeline specification.
- [[summaries/instruction_fetch_rst]] (short) — This document serves as a source map detailing the structure of instruction fetching, memory interfaces, branch prediction, and access handling protocols.
- [[summaries/pipeline_details]] (short) — This page provides a Graphify-derived, curated view of a component entity candidate for OpenKB input.
- [[summaries/instruction_fetch]] (short) — This document defines a component anchor for instruction fetch used as compact input for OpenKB.
- [[summaries/00_graphify_spec_wiki_index]] (short) — This wiki serves as a compact, graph-derived index for the Graphify specification, prioritizing data retention and curation.

## Concepts
- [[concepts/topic-memory]] — The Memory Topic Cluster defines the identity and curation guidelines for the 'memory' topic extracted from the spec graph.
- [[concepts/pipeline-stages----Pipeline-Stages]] — Pipeline stages define the structural components and specific instructions governing the flow of data through the pipeline.
- [[concepts/protocol-instruction-fetch]] — The Instruction Fetch Protocol governs instruction retrieval coordinated across the pipeline stages and memory access interfaces.
- [[concepts/misaligned-accesses]] — Misaligned memory accesses refer to handling memory accesses that do not adhere to standard alignment boundaries.
- [[concepts/instruction-side-memory-interface]] — The Instruction-Side Memory Interface defines the mechanism for accessing memory directly from the instruction stream.
- [[concepts/branch-prediction]] — This document maps the specifications for instruction fetching, branch prediction, memory interfaces, and access protocols.
- [[concepts/instruction-fetch]] — The Instruction Fetch Mechanism retrieves instructions, incorporating details about pipeline stages and instruction cycle types.</data>
